# Project: BuzzPrint (Georgia Tech Campus Action & Proof-of-Work Network)

## Overview & Core Concept
Build a responsive, web-first campus platform called **BuzzPrint** for Georgia Tech ("See what's happening on campus right now. Leave your BuzzPrint.")[cite: 1]. Instead of a passive campus directory, BuzzPrint is a live, spatial ecosystem connecting students, campus spaces, and alumni through real-time action and verified "Proof-of-Work" portfolios[cite: 1].

We are building a polished, interactive vertical slice centered around **The Kendeda Building for Innovative Sustainable Design** (422 Ferst Dr NW, Atlanta, GA) for a pitch competition demo.

---

## Architecture & UI Layout (Strict 3-Column Desktop / Responsive Mobile)
Use a clean, modern tech-forward UI (Georgia Tech Navy `#003057`, Tech Gold `#B3A369`, crisp white/slate cards, subtle shadows). Organize the main dashboard into **3 primary columns**:

### 1. Left Column: Interactive Campus & Building Map
- **Map View:** Interactive 2D/isometric campus map centered on **The Kendeda Building** (with nearby Eco-Commons and Instructional Center context).
- **Layer Toggles (Top Bar):**
  1. `Live Beacons & Bounties` (Study groups, club events, skill requests)
  2. `Spaces & Crowd Density` (Floor-by-floor room availability & capacity)[cite: 2]
  3. `Maintenance Triage` (Active facility/IT pins)[cite: 2]
  4. `Built Here (BuzzPrint History)` (Verified student projects/milestones completed in the building)[cite: 2]
- **Skill Filter Bar:** Allow alumni/recruiters or students to filter map pins and student builders by skill tags (e.g., `Python`, `CAD / 3D Printing`, `React`, `Sustainability`, `UI/UX`)[cite: 2].

### 2. Middle Column: Action Dashboard & BuzzPrint Portfolio
Include a clean tab switcher at the top of the middle column:
- **Tab 1: Live Feed (Beacons, Bounties & Events)**
  - Filterable feed of active study beacons (e.g., *"Working on CS 3510 Algo at Atrium North Table — 2 seats open"*), club meetups, and micro-bounties (e.g., *"SOS Club needs a Figma designer for Earth Day graphics"*)[cite: 2].
  - **"Drop a Pin / Post Bounty" Button:** Opens a quick modal to drop a new beacon or bounty at a specific Kendeda floor/room with skill tags.
  - **"Claim / Complete" Flow:** Clicking "Complete & Verify" on a bounty triggers a 1-click verification toast and immediately logs that item into the active user's **BuzzPrint Portfolio**[cite: 2].
- **Tab 2: My BuzzPrint (Proof-of-Work Portfolio)**
  - Auto-generated visual record of the user's GT campus involvement (tied to simulated GT SSO login)[cite: 1].
  - **Stats Header:** Total BuzzPrint Score, Buildings Frequented, Bounties Completed, Maintenance Fixes Verified.
  - **Verified Work Cards:** Displays completed projects, study milestones, and resolved tickets with location badges (`@ Kendeda Building`), skill tags, and verifier stamps (e.g., *"Verified by Students Organizing for Sustainability"*).
- **Tab 3: Smart Maintenance Reporter**
  - Single-entry form: Upload/select photo, auto-tagged GPS coordinates + building/floor selector, issue description, and category (or an `"I have no idea — broadcast to ops"` button).
  - **5-Meter Auto-Merge Logic:** Simulate proximity detection! If a user submits a ticket within 5 meters of an existing active ticket (e.g., a broken water bottle refill sensor on Kendeda Floor 1), automatically merge it into the existing ticket, increment the `Report Count` badge, and show a confirmation banner instead of creating a duplicate.

### 3. Right Column: Contextual Deep-Dive Drawer
Dynamically updates based on what the user clicks in the Left or Middle column:
- **Default / Building View (Kendeda Building):**
  - Header with Kendeda Building photo, Living Building Challenge 3.1 badge, operating hours, BuzzCard access status, and live floor-by-floor crowd density meters (`Basement: Quiet 15%`, `Floor 1 Atrium: Lively 65%`, `Floor 2 Study Rooms: Moderate 40%`, `Rooftop Garden: Open 20%`).
  - **Upgraded Room Reservations:** List of Kendeda spaces (`Atrium Open Tables`, `Breakout Room 212`, `Seminar Room 230`, `Rooftop Terrace`) showing real room preview photos, exact seating capacity, outlet density, whiteboard/AV specs, noise/privacy level, and a 1-click **Reserve Slot** button[cite: 2].
  - **Active Builders & Alumni Bridge:** Shows students currently checked into Kendeda beacons and a "Scout Talent" preview showing how alumni/founders view verified student builders[cite: 2].
- **Profile / Pin Detail View:** Clicking any user or bounty opens their full **BuzzPrint** card or bounty details with a direct "Connect / Message" action[cite: 2].

